# GMS's decoy, cut down to the one thing this game can read: damage on a clock.
# Its health bar, the counterattack it launches when struck, and the stun are
# all dropped -- nothing here draws aggro, so a decoy that holds it is a decoy
# doing nothing.
#
# Six enemies rather than GMS's eight, and its top 200% reached at 20 levels
# rather than 30. Stripped of everything but the damage it would otherwise
# crowd out Frostprey, which is the Sniper's whole summon.
#
# Three seconds between strikes, watched rather than read: GMS states no rate
# for it, and unlike Phoenix it carries no cadence in its animation either.
name: "Arrow Illusion"
skill_order: 4
description:
  "Summons an arrow illusion that damages enemies on its own. Also increases "
  "Ignore Defense permanently."
kind: SKILL_KIND_AUTO_ATTACK
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN
max_level: 20
exceeds_master_level: true
max_enemies: 6
cast_interval_seconds: 3.0
base {
  skill_pct: 1.05
  ied_pct: 0.015
}
per_level {
  skill_pct: 0.05
  ied_pct: 0.015
}
